# Validation
Build configuration version: 3. Selected C sources and their library dependencies
are unchanged from FFmpeg "'`1019f8f036`. No compiled shim changes, so no full C/FATE
baseline is required for this wrap batch.
The shared ASan/UBSan and TSan builds name Clang 20.1.2; the shared coverage
build names GCC 14.2.0. Those compilers are not present in this execution
environment (Clang 18.1.3 and GCC 13.3.0 are present). Consequently private,
agent-unique libavutil replacements were built in `/tmp/crypto-b8/builds/`:
```
<worktree>/configure --enable-shared --disable-static --disable-autodetect '"\\
  --enable-pthreads --enable-zlib --disable-doc --disable-stripping \\
  --samples=/target/crustify/fate-suite <variant-options>
make -j8 libavutil/libavutil.so
"'```
Variant options: `--toolchain=clang-asan-ubsan --cc=/usr/bin/clang-18`,
`--toolchain=clang-tsan --cc=/usr/bin/clang-18`, and
`--toolchain=gcov --cc=/usr/bin/gcc`. Other untouched link-unit libraries are
symlinked from the matching campaign variant solely to link the workspace;
all authored FFI calls and existing safe APIs currently target the private
libavutil. The campaign builds were never modified. Coverage uses private
`GCOV_PREFIX`/`LLVM_PROFILE_FILE` outputs.
The immutable BSan prebuild matches the installed compiler exactly:
Clang 23.1.3-rust-1.101.0-nightly, LLVM revision
`aab11ee0ea5ea9a1d462ad0bc1fae9d9bb643019`, with the campaign BSan plugin.
## Completed evidence
- Affected `libavutil-sys` bindings regenerated by its build script; no new shim
  or input header was necessary.
- Static scan: `crustify scan-unsafe <worktree>/crustify/rust/ffmpeg --json --sites all`.
  `scan-unsafe.json` retains full-crate counts and only this worklist'"'s sites.
  Both layout wrappers are conformant. All pointer/unsafe function sites for
  these TUs are sanctioned ffibox seams; no worklist smell was found. The four
  authored FFI calls are internal, with specific safety comments.
- BSan ran **only** exact names
  "'`tea::constructors_and_exclusive_reinitialization` and
  `twofish::constructors_and_exclusive_reinitialization`, each separately
  through `cargo bsan test -p ffmpeg --test ub_safe <name> -- --exact`, under
  a 600-second timeout, with `CRUSTIFY_FFMPEG_VARIANT=bsan`. Both passed.
- Miri passed `libavutil::twofish::unit_tests::validation_and_errors` and both
  `layout_matches_ffi` unit tests. Foreign construction/drop tests are excluded
  under Miri, which cannot execute C. No new public unsafe functions require
  an ub_unsafe suite; ffibox raw adoption is covered by internal unit fixtures.
- Coverage: focused unit, ub_safe and equiv tests ran against the private
  coverage library and Rust `-C instrument-coverage` (nightly). Authored
  non-test Rust executable lines: TEA **8/8**, Twofish **33/33**. Whole selected
  C TUs: TEA **52/52** lines, **22/22** branches executed and taken;
  Twofish **164/164** lines, **226/226** branches executed and taken.
  Detailed results are in `coverage.json`. The environment-dependent allocator
  failure alternatives remain unforced; forcing the process-wide allocator
  limit would interfere with concurrent safe API tests. No reachable uncovered
  source line remains. Cipher coverage is generated by C readers in equiv,
  not by adding out-of-worklist cipher wrappers.
Detailed agent-unique build/test logs and profiles are under `/tmp/crypto-b8/`.
EOF
