    "_comment_agent": "C enum (int-backed, AV_SAMPLE_FMT_NONE = -1 .. AV_SAMPLE_FMT_NB = 12): no fields, no pointers, no lifecycle. Stored by value in public fields users write directly (AVCodecContext.sample_fmt / request_sample_fmt, AVFrame.format as int, AVOption AV_OPT_TYPE_SAMPLE_FMT targets) and in AV_SAMPLE_FMT_NONE-terminated arrays (AVCodec.sample_fmts), so any int is an observable value; libavutil/samplefmt.c and swresample bound-check with `< 0 || >= AV_SAMPLE_FMT_NB` before table lookups. Wrapped as an open #[repr(transparent)] newtype (SampleFormat) accepting every int; plain element (CPlainElem) for av_malloc arrays.",
    "fields": []
   },
+  {
+   "name": "AVTEA",
+   "defined_in": "libavutil/tea.c",
+   "_comment_agent": "AVTEA is opaque in its public header; all fields are inline integers/arrays, no pointer fields, resources, clone routine, retain or transfer. av_tea_alloc uses av_mallocz, the caller owns it and av_free/av_freep releases it. Init copies key bytes and retains no argument pointer. Crypt reads the initialized schedule only. C remains layout/storage owner; no public fields and no field accessors.",
